1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,800
Label Loop is a working online classifier inside a web page.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:11,000
It starts with nine support tickets and learns new billing,
bug, and access examples during the session.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,208
No backend or model API is involved.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:23,200
Chrome exposes WebMCP on this deployed page,
and the green badge confirms nine registered tools.

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:30,500
The browser agent receives typed operations for training,
evaluation, learned-model diagnostics, and direct inference.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:38,392
It can query the model without interpreting the page layout.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
For this recorded run, I use the labeled local replay
so each step is predictable and easy to inspect.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,100
It calls the same production handlers.

9
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:57,100
The first calls read aggregate state and rank the unlabeled pool
by normalized predictive entropy.

10
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:03,144
High entropy means the class probabilities are close,
so these tickets are useful candidates for human review.

11
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:09,900
The replay requests two labels,
but the tool schema has no label field.

12
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:16,000
I assign the authoritative categories on the page.
Until I do that, the training tool rejects these samples.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,896
Agent predictions cannot become training truth
without this human action.

14
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:28,200
On the next turn, the model increments its document and token counts
with my confirmed examples.

15
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:33,900
Predictions are recalculated immediately.

16
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:39,700
Diagnostics expose one-versus-rest token weights, aggregate confusion
counts, confidence calibration, log loss, and per-class scores.

17
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:45,012
Individual holdout answers are not returned to the agent.

18
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:52,300
The agent can recommend a different Laplace smoothing value
and low-confidence review threshold.

19
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:58,900
The proposal appears beside the review queue
and has no effect until I accept it.

20
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:05,356
After approval, the threshold controls whether a new prediction
is safe to route or should go to a person.

21
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,200
I can now test the current classifier with fresh text.
A clear export failure routes to the bug class with enough confidence.

22
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:18,500
An ambiguous payment and login report stays below the approved threshold
and is marked for human review.

23
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:24,720
The decision uses the model state we just changed.

24
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:31,700
The trace keeps WebMCP reads and writes visible.

25
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:37,600
The ledger separates agent requests, human labels, and model updates.

26
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:43,460
Label Loop is deployed as a static app. The live site,
source, contracts, and tests are ready for judge review.
